+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry owns validation of the same JSON Schema it exposes to providers, so executors can rely on accepted input.
+
+## Contract
+
+- `execute` rejects missing required fields, incorrect declared types and invalid enum members before invoking the executor, returning a `ToolResponse` with property paths and constraints but no input values in either diagnostics or logs; valid input, including unknown keys, reaches the executor exactly once without coercion or defaults, and an unknown tool still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`. ([validated by: rejects invalid tool input privately and passes valid input unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L22))
+- Static schemas are compiled during registration, invalid schemas throw with the tool name at registration, and ten later calls reuse the compiled schema without reading it again. ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and reuses them across ten calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L79))
+- Function-valued definitions resolve on each execution and use the current schema, caching compilation by schema object identity rather than tool name. ([validated by: validates each dynamic definition using its current cached schema object](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L118))
+
+## Integration and release obligations
+
+The execute doc comment points here and remains one line. Validation rejection is a tool result available to the model for correction within the existing five-tool-round budget, rather than a transport exception. Existing executor exceptions are not schema rejections.
+
+Use a JSON Schema validator in runtime dependencies. README.md, docs/adding-a-tool.md and .specify/spec.md must explain accepted inputs, unchanged extra properties, and rejection results. Publish a MINOR version and a consumer-facing CHANGELOG.md migration note explaining that executors no longer receive schema-invalid input; repeat the migration note in the PR body. CI owns build, package import, type, lint and formatting verification.
